\tag{fdip}
\title{Spectral triples and induced distance}
\date{2026-11-02}

\p{Can a distance on a finite set be read from an operator, rather than
from edge weights supplied with the complex?}

\p{On three points the commutator of a real symmetric matrix with a
function determines the distance by a closed formula. On the path of
4 vertices that distance is #{2}, while the graph distance is
#{3}. The following section proves both evaluations. The section
after it takes up operators that see the edges.}

\transclude{fdip-0095}
